course: dictionary
lesson: 13015
title: Extremity: the far edges
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An extremity is the far end or edge of something. It can also mean the far parts of your body, like your fingers and toes. «In the frost, the cold bit first at his extremities, and his fingers went numb.» The clues are frost and numb, so extremities must mean the parts furthest from the middle of the body.
explain: Read the words around it. «The ship sailed to the northern extremity of the island.» The word northern tells you where: it is the far north edge. Ask yourself what word would fit. Edge fits, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Sometimes extremity means a very serious or dangerous situation. «The climbers faced the extremity of the storm, but they stayed together.» Storm and stayed together are the clues, so this is the formal meaning. Extremity is a noun: one extremity, many extremities.
fact: An extremity is a noun, so you can have one extremity or many extremities.
fact: «Extremities» can mean the far parts of your body, such as hands, feet, fingers and toes.
fact: «Extremity» can mean the far end or edge of a place, such as the northern extremity of a country.
fact: In formal writing, «extremity» can mean a very serious or dangerous situation.
fact: In cold weather, frostbite often affects the extremities first, which is why fingers and toes get cold so quickly.
exercise: «In cold weather, frostbite often affects the extremities first.» What are the extremities in this sentence? | The middle of your back | *Fingers and toes | Your school bag | Eyes and ears
exercise: «The northern extremity of the island is rocky.» What does extremity mean here? | *The far end or edge | A small pond | The very middle | A type of boat
exercise: «The crew faced the extremity of the storm.» What does extremity suggest? | *A very serious, dangerous situation | A sunny beach | A short song | A cosy warm room
test: Lily's fingers were cold, and her extremities were numb. What are her extremities? | Her heart and lungs | *Her fingers and toes | Her school bag | The middle of her back
test: «The hikers were in extremity after the storm cut off their path.» What does extremity mean here? | Mild, sunny weather | A soft bed | *A very serious, dangerous situation | A short walk
exam: «The map marked the northern extremity of the country.» What does this tell the reader? | It shows the middle of the country | It shows a big city | It shows a river | *It shows the far northern edge
